# Everything a build context does not need. Without this the context for the
# `blobstore` image alone is roughly a gigabyte — `blobstore/target` is 800 MB of
# incremental Rust artefacts on its own — and every `docker build` pays for it.

.git/
.gradle/
build/
*/build/
**/target/
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
deploy/secrets/
docs/
# ...except the one file the APPLICATION reads at runtime. `docs/reference/` is
# the source of truth for the shipped item type templates (REQ-CORE-030) and the
# build copies it into the artifact; excluded from the context, the copy found
# nothing, the jar shipped without it, and `api` refused to start inside the
# image while every test on the host passed. The smoke suite caught it, which is
# what the smoke suite is for.
!docs/reference/type-templates.yaml
website/
design-system/
*.md
